From: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@linux.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Release the Firestore core before its cleanup notifier

~FirestoreInternal disposes of the core and leaves the rest to member
destruction.  firestore_core_ is declared before cleanup_, so cleanup_ is
destroyed first.  The core's SyncEngine holds the callbacks of writes still
pending, and each holds a Promise registered with cleanup_.

Firestore::DeleteInternal() runs cleanup_.CleanupAll(), which resets every
Promise registered then and marks the notifier cleaned up.  The worker queue
runs until Dispose(), and a write's callback moved on it after that registers
the moved Promise again.  ~CleanupNotifier calls CleanupAll(), which does
nothing the second time, so that Promise keeps a pointer to the notifier.
When the core goes, ~SyncEngine destroys the callback and the Promise
unregisters from freed memory: "corrupted size vs. prev_size" or a double
free on Linux, 0xC0000409 on Windows.

Deleting an App with a write in flight is enough.  Release the core at the
end of the destructor, while cleanup_ is alive.
---
 firestore/src/main/firestore_main.cc | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/firestore/src/main/firestore_main.cc b/firestore/src/main/firestore_main.cc
index f2aacca..28df442 100644
--- a/firestore/src/main/firestore_main.cc
+++ b/firestore/src/main/firestore_main.cc
@@ -133,6 +133,13 @@ FirestoreInternal::~FirestoreInternal() {
   ClearListeners();
   transaction_executor_->Dispose();
   firestore_core_->Dispose();
+  // Release the core while `cleanup_` is alive. It holds the callbacks of
+  // writes still pending, and each holds a Promise registered with `cleanup_`.
+  // Members go in reverse order, so left to them `cleanup_` is gone first, and
+  // a Promise registered after Firestore::DeleteInternal() ran CleanupAll()
+  // unregisters from freed memory. CleanupAll() runs only once, and the queue
+  // moves callbacks, registering the moved Promise, until Dispose() returns.
+  firestore_core_.reset();
 }
 
 std::shared_ptr<api::Firestore> FirestoreInternal::CreateFirestore(
